{"ISBN:9780156013369":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780156013369","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL22467395M/Postville","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL22467395M/Postville","details":{"publishers":["Harcourt"],"identifiers":{"librarything":["7761686"],"goodreads":["142826"]},"subtitle":"a clash of cultures in heartland America","isbn_10":["0156013363"],"local_id":["urn:cst:10017004886","urn:bwbsku:P7-BTR-162"],"lc_classifications":["F630.J5 B56 2000","","F630.J5 B56 2001"],"key":"/books/OL22467395M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL1476276A","name":"Stephen G. Bloom"}],"publish_places":["San Diego"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"pagination":"xiv, 362 p. ;","source_records":["marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_barcode.mrc:22023215:2816","bwb:9780156013369","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_multibarcode.mrc:22032906:2816","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-05-17"],"title":"Postville","dewey_decimal_class":["977.7/33"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Updated with a new afterword\". Cover.\n\n\"A Harvest book\"."},"number_of_pages":362,"edition_name":"1st Harvest ed.","subjects":["Bloom, Stephen G.","Jews -- Iowa -- Postville -- History.","Hasidim -- Iowa -- Postville -- History.","Postville (Iowa) -- Ethnic relations.","Postville (Iowa) -- Politics and government."],"publish_date":"2001","publish_country":"cau","by_statement":"Stephen G. Bloom.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL5952523W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"latest_revision":9,"revision":9,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-11-14T13:33:24.188690"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-12-08T11:34:54.432218"}}},"ISBN:9780151006526":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780151006526","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7362514M/Postville","preview":"borrow","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/postvilleclashof00bloo_0","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/112235-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Harcourt"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["1241726"],"librarything":["7761686"]},"subtitle":"A Clash of Cultures in Heartland America","ia_box_id":["IA175101"],"isbn_10":["0151006520"],"covers":[112235],"ia_loaded_id":["postvilleclashof00bloo_0"],"key":"/books/OL7362514M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL1476276A","name":"Stephen G. Bloom"}],"ocaid":"postvilleclashof00bloo_0","languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"source_records":["amazon:0151006520:11:3185796796:259860","marc:marc_loc_updates/v37.i52.records.utf8:33123:1009","ia:postvilleclashof00bloo_0","marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run02.mrc:211337470:1834","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part01.utf8:23175746:1009","bwb:9780151006526","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-08-29","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-006.mrc:257590884:2101","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_027.bib.mrc:71529112:1811"],"title":"Postville","lccn":["00038928"],"number_of_pages":352,"isbn_13":["9780151006526"],"local_id":["urn:sfpl:31223056446678","urn:sfpl:31223056446629","urn:bwbsku:W7-CQU-158"],"publish_date":"October 2, 2000","works":[{"key":"/works/OL5952523W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The only time I had ever been in Iowa was when I was a fourteen-year-old Boy Scout on the way to Philmont Scout Ranch in New Mexico, and our horny troop spent the night in a dormitory at Iowa State University on the lookout all evening for sex-crazed college coeds we never found."},"lc_classifications":["F630.J5B56 2000","F630.J5 B56 2000"],"oclc_numbers":["43903695"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"In 1987, a group of Lubavitchers, one of the most orthodox and zealous of Jewish sects, opened a kosher slaughterhouse just outside tiny Postville, Iowa (pop. 1,465). When the business became a worldwide success, Postville found itself both revived and divided. The town's initial welcome of the Jews turned into confusion, dismay, and even disgust. By 1997, the town had engineered a vote on what everyone agreed was actually a referendum: whether or not these Jews should stay.\".\n\n\"Stephen G. Bloom found himself with a bird's-eye view of this battle and gained a new perspective on questions that haunt America nationwide. What makes a community? How does one accept new and powerfully different traditions? Is money more important than history? In the dramatic and often poignant stories of the people of Postville - Jew and gentile, puzzled and puzzling, unyielding and unstoppable - lies a great swath of America today.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":16,"revision":16,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T13:35:46.876380"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-01-11T22:00:15.252742"}}},"ISBN:9789650502249":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9789650502249","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL2299730M/Toratah_shel_ha-Ḥasidut","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL2299730M/Toratah_shel_ha-Ḥasidut","details":{"other_titles":["Hasidic thought."],"publishers":["Maṭkal/Ḳetsin ḥinukh rashi/Gale Tsahal, Miśrad ha-biṭaḥon"],"isbn_10":["9650502246"],"series":["Sifriyat \"universiṭah meshuderet\"","Sifriyat universiṭah meshuderet."],"lc_classifications":["BM198 .J373 1985"],"key":"/books/OL2299730M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL1041182A","name":"Yoram Jacobson"}],"publish_places":["[Tel Aviv]"],"contributions":["Zevulun, Taʼir."],"pagination":"147 p. :","source_records":["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part19.dat:16207442:838","marc:marc_loc_updates/v37.i42.records.utf8:15340465:876","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part17.utf8:128869426:876","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.00.20150123.full.mrc:406481274:932","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-002.mrc:197787963:1950"],"title":"Toratah shel ha-Ḥasidut","lccn":["86172275"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Bibliography: p. [146]-147.\nTitle on t.p. verso: The Hasidic thought."},"number_of